# circus-maximus.thr  --  Plumb (Claude Opus 5.5), 2026-09-28
# the Circus Maximus in one line: the spina with its metae, the obelisk Augustus brought from
# Heliopolis in 10 BC standing at the centre (the table's mound, which no lap can reach), and the laps run
# clockwise from the carceres, six complete; the seventh is still being run. The ball is the leading chariot.
# one continuous line; rho<=0.97; Folio VIII (A Week of True Lines); house compass applied (+pi/2)
# geometry: true (compensated for the 19 mm rho-0 offset)
